---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
	title="Software for community pottery studios"
	description="Kilnbook runs shared wheels, firing queues and memberships for community pottery studios, so members can book, log work and see when it is out of the kiln."
>
	<section class="band-dark page-hero">
		<div class="wrap split">
			<div>
				<p class="eyebrow">Community studios</p>
				<h1>Shared wheels, shared kilns, one front desk.</h1>
				<p class="lede">
					Members log their own pieces into the firing queue, book wheels and tables within the limits
					of their membership, and get a text when their work is ready. You stop being the go-between.
				</p>
				<a href="/contact" class="btn">Book a demo</a>
			</div>
			<img
				src="/images/wheel-grid.svg"
				alt="A day view of four wheels booked in one-hour blocks from 9am to 6pm"
				width="480"
				height="300"
			/>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section section-alt">
		<div class="wrap">
			<p class="eyebrow">Sound familiar?</p>
			<h2>What the front desk hears every week</h2>
			<div class="cards">
				<div class="card">
					<h3>"Is my bowl out yet?"</h3>
					<p>
						Members want to know where their work is, and the only way to find out is to ask you or
						check the shelf.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="card">
					<h3>"Someone's on my wheel."</h3>
					<p>
						Evenings and weekends fill up first, and a sign-up sheet does not know who is on which
						membership.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="card">
					<h3>"Who paid for this firing?"</h3>
					<p>
						The kiln log is on a clipboard, the payments are in an app, and matching them up eats your
						weekend.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap section narrow">
		<h2>Built for a studio full of members</h2>
		<p>
			A community studio runs on shared equipment and a lot of people working on their own schedule.
			Kilnbook keeps the wheels, the kilns and the memberships in one place, so the rules you set are
			the rules members see.
		</p>

		<h2>Wheel time by membership tier</h2>
		<p>
			Members reserve wheels, hand-building tables and the slab roller in one-hour blocks. You decide
			how many hours each tier gets and how far ahead they can book. Freed-up slots go back on the
			calendar as soon as someone cancels. <a href="/features/wheel-time">How wheel booking works</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>A firing queue members can see</h2>
		<p>
			Members log a piece from their phone when they set it on the bisque shelf. Kilnbook charges the
			firing fee by cubic inch, puts it in the right load and texts them when it is ready for pickup.
			The kiln log is the invoice. <a href="/features/firings">How firing queues work</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Know who is in the building</h2>
		<p>
			Put a tablet by the door for open studio check-in. Members tap their name when they arrive, so
			you always know who is in, which matters when the kilns are running.
		</p>

		<h2>Classes and packs too</h2>
		<p>
			Most community studios teach as well. Sell courses, drop-ins and class packs from the same
			account, with waitlists that offer cancelled seats to the next person on their own.
			<a href="/features/classes">Classes and packs</a>.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="band-dark quote-band">
		<div class="wrap split">
			<blockquote class="quote">
				[Quote from a community studio owner about running members, wheels and firings on Kilnbook]
				<cite>[Name, role, studio (city)]</cite>
			</blockquote>
			<div>
				<p class="eyebrow">Proof</p>
				<h2>Started in a community studio</h2>
				<p>
					Kilnbook began in a 14-wheel community studio in Portland. Over 340 studios in the US,
					Canada and the UK now run their bookings, firings and memberships on it.
				</p>
				<p>[Result a community studio saw after switching to Kilnbook, with a number]</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="cta-band">
		<div class="wrap">
			<h2>Give your members their own front desk.</h2>
			<p>30 days free on the Studio plan. No card to start, and nothing is deleted if you walk away.</p>
			<a href="/contact" class="btn btn-dark">Book a demo</a>
		</div>
	</section>
</Base>
